  "AgentEval, a DAG-structured step-level judge, reached failure-detection recall 0.89 on 150 human-annotated cases versus 0.41 for end-to-end-only evaluation and 0.67 for flat step-level evaluation, at FPR 0.07 versus 0.08 and 0.15.": 1,
  "In the AgentEval study, 63% of step-level failures across 450 test cases were propagated from upstream errors rather than locally caused, and the DAG advantage over flat evaluation grew from +15 pp for workflows of ≤3 steps to +28 pp for ≥6 steps.": 1
 }
